  "title": "Epilepsy-iEEG-Interictal-Multicenter-Dataset",
  "description": "A multicenter dataset of interictal intracranial EEG (iEEG) recordings from de-identified epilepsy patients, with sleep or awake state annotated where available. Data come from NIH, Johns Hopkins Hospital and University of Miami Jackson Memorial Hospital, and include patients treated with resection/ablation or responsive neurostimulation (RNS). Derivatives include source-sink connectivity analyses and high-frequency oscillation (HFO) detections using RMS and Hilbert detectors.",
  "methods_description": "Intracranial EEG recordings were collected during interictal periods from subjects with epilepsy across multiple clinical centers. Data were de-identified and organized according to BIDS and iEEG-BIDS specifications using MNE-BIDS. Sleep and awake states were annotated where available. High-frequency oscillations were detected using both RMS and Hilbert transform methods.",
